# Accessibility checklist (WCAG 2.2 AA, every platform)

Run this before reporting any UI change. A box that does not apply is skipped, not ticked. The computed contrast evidence
for every colour pair, in both themes, is in [dark-mode.md](dark-mode.md).

## Everywhere

- [ ] Text contrast at least 4.5:1 (3:1 for large text); control boundaries and focus indicators at least 3:1, in light and dark.
- [ ] Meaning is never colour alone: status is a word plus an icon.
- [ ] Every control reachable and usable by keyboard (web) or switch/screen reader (mobile), in a logical order.
- [ ] A visible focus indicator on every control, not hidden by other content.
- [ ] Every control has an accessible name; icon-only controls are labelled; decorative images are hidden from assistive tech.
- [ ] Form fields have labels; errors are linked to their field and announced; instructions are not placeholder-only.
- [ ] Touch targets at least 44pt (iOS), 48dp (Android), 44px on touch web layouts; 24px minimum with spacing on pointer layouts.
- [ ] Nothing depends on hover alone; nothing needs a gesture without a single-pointer alternative.
- [ ] Reduced motion respected; no flashing more than three times a second; no auto-playing motion over 5 seconds without a pause.
- [ ] Text can be enlarged (200% web, largest Dynamic Type or font scale on mobile) without loss of content or function.
- [ ] Dialogs and sheets trap focus, close on Escape or back, and return focus to the trigger.
- [ ] Status changes (toasts, saves, errors) are announced politely without moving focus.
- [ ] Language is set; headings are in order; one main landmark per page (web).

## Web

- [ ] Native elements first (`button`, `a`, `input`); ARIA only to fill a gap, and the pattern's full keyboard model.
- [ ] Skip link to the main content; page title changes on navigation.
- [ ] Layout holds at 320px wide and with text spacing increased.

## iOS

- [ ] VoiceOver reads each element once, in order, with traits (button, selected); custom actions for swipe actions.
- [ ] Dynamic Type up to the largest accessibility size; no truncation of essential text.

## Android

- [ ] TalkBack reads each element once, in order, with role and state; `contentDescription` on icon-only controls.
- [ ] Font scale up to 200%; predictive back works.
